/*! \page e3_wire E3 Wire Guide

Git Markdown companion: \c docs/dapp/e3_wire.md (normative prose).
Normative schemas: \c schemas/e3/e3sm-ocudu-dapp-mgmt-v1.asn1,
\c schemas/e3/e3ap-ocudu-v1.asn1, \c schemas/e3/e3sm-ocudu-telemetry-v1.asn1,
\c schemas/e3/e3sm-ocudu-dapp-mgmt-carrier-v1.asn1 (all ASN.1 Aligned PER) and
\c schemas/dapp/e3-data-profile-v1.fbs (FlatBuffers compatibility carrier).

\section e3_wire_carriers Carriers

- **Local management** (\c dapp.local_e3): \c AF_UNIX \c SOCK_SEQPACKET, one
  APER \c ManagementRequest per datagram, \c SO_PEERCRED UID admission, no
  length prefix, 2 MiB bound.
- **E3AP** (\c dapp.e3ap_sctp): SCTP one-to-one association, one \c E3-PDU per
  SCTP message (\c MSG_EOR framing), stream 0 procedures / stream 1
  indications, default port 36423. Setup, subscription, push indications,
  management as control actions, release.
- **E3 data profile** (\c dapp.e3dp_sctp): SCTP, size-prefixed FlatBuffers
  \c E3DP, \c dataSubscriptions / \c dataPoll only, default port 38472, for the
  standalone E3 SCTP reference client.

All carriers share \ref ocudu::dapp::e3::management_service and
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::portable_data_store.

\section e3_wire_primitives Primitives

Identifiers are 16-byte \c OCTET STRING values. Hashes are 32 raw bytes.
Bounded text is UTF-8 carried as \c OCTET STRING (never \c UTF8String, whose
size constraints are not PER-visible and diverge between encoders); malformed
UTF-8 is rejected. 64-bit counters are 8-byte network-order octets. Every
SEQUENCE and ENUMERATED is extensible.

\section e3_wire_e3ap E3AP envelope

\c E3-PDU carries an \c id (echoed as \c requestId) and a CHOICE over
\c setupRequest, \c setupResponse, \c subscriptionRequest,
\c subscriptionDelete, \c subscriptionResponse, \c indicationMessage,
\c dAppControlAction, \c dAppReport, \c xAppControlAction, \c releaseMessage,
\c messageAck and \c controlResponse. Service-model bodies are opaque APER
octets selected by \c ranFunctionIdentifier: 10 = \c OCUDU-TELEMETRY-SM,
11 = \c E3SM-OCUDU-DAPP-MGMT-V1. Payloads above 64 KiB are fragmented at the
E3AP layer (\c fragmentIndex, \c fragmentCount, \c payloadBytes) and
reassembled by PDU id (control) or subscription id plus sequence (indication).

\section e3_wire_telemetry Telemetry service model

Telemetry identifiers 1..8: \c pusch.symbols, \c pusch.crc, \c srs.channel,
\c pusch.dmrs_channel, \c gnb.metrics_json, \c classc.spectrum,
\c classc.srs_isac, \c pusch.grid (store interface \c 0x00020006).
\c Telemetry-IndicationData carries the stream id, cell,
sequence, route epoch, monotonic timestamp, cumulative drop counter and one
\c Telemetry-Object. Complex vectors are little-endian binary32 (re, im) pairs.
Subscription filters (\c Telemetry-SubscriptionConfig: cell, sampleEveryN,
drop policy, minimum interval, RNTI list) travel in
\c E3-SubscriptionRequest.subscriptionData. Requested capture intervals are
per RNTI; a stream's advertised \c hardFloorIntervalUs is an aggregate
per-stream bound no subscriber can go below. The management service model
additionally offers \c ranControl (UE release, handover, RU TX/RX gain) and
\c cellInfo (served cells plus RAN-control capabilities), and its inventory
lists the current downstream E3 connections.

\section e3_wire_store Packed store metadata

Telemetry publications in the portable store start with the 16-byte
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::telemetry_metadata_header (magic \c 0x3345544F,
version 1 or 2, kind 1..6, monotonic ns) followed by the kind-specific packed
record defined in \c include/ocudu/dapp/e3/telemetry_types.h. \c pusch.symbols
is published as version 2 (152 bytes: v1 record, capture flags, grant block);
\c pusch.grid is kind 6 (120 bytes including the same grant block); every
other kind stays version 1. The RNTI always follows the header so RNTI
filters need no codec.

\section e3_wire_interop Interoperability

The E3AP module mirrors the libe3 procedure set and field names but is not
byte-compatible with libe3 (which lacks extension markers, bounds identifiers to
1..100 and payloads to 32 KiB, and answers control actions with a bare ack).
NVIDIA cuSense uses JSON over ZMQ. The reference SCTP client tarball carries a
trimmed Class-C schema with renumbered enumerators; regenerate it from the
normative OCUDU schema before interop.

\section e3_wire_security Security

No TLS or token authentication in v1. Bind loopback or add an external
boundary; \c allowed_peers narrows admission to literal addresses. E3AP
management control actions carry full management authority.

\section e3_wire_related Related

\ref e3_management, \ref e3_system_design, \ref dapp_observability.
*/
